## Context

Eight command sections in the manual reference "auto-discovered tickets/" as the
default DIR, but never explain what auto-discovery means. An agent reading only the
manual cannot determine which directory `erg` will use when no DIR is given.

The actual logic (from the code): erg tries (1) directory containing the binary,
(2) `tickets/` under CWD, (3) CWD itself. A directory qualifies if it is named
`tickets`, contains `.erg-bootstrap-manifest.json`, or contains at least one `.erg` file.

## Actions
1. Add a short paragraph to the intro section of `--help --all` output (in `main.go`)
   explaining store auto-discovery, or add a dedicated `## Store discovery` section.
2. Alternatively, add a note to the first command that uses a DIR default (`erg check`)
   and cross-reference it from other commands.
3. Run `make test && make docs`.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Manual explains what "auto-discovered tickets/" means
- [ ] The four-step resolution order is documented
- [ ] What qualifies as a valid store is stated
- [ ] `make test` passes
